DESCRIPTION:Topic: A special civic meetup: Post-election recap!\n\nResiden
 ts go to the polls on Monday Oct 26th\, and the next evening we're hosting
  a special discussion\, to reflect on the results\, the issues\, and the s
 urprises along the way\, which made this election memorable.\n\nSpeakers: 
 Anita Li\, Matt Elliott and Lanrick Bennett Jr. (moderator)\n\nAnita Li is
  the publisher and CEO of The Green Line\, an award-winning community-driv
 en news outlet in Toronto\, and recently served as Journalism Innovator-in
 -Residence at Toronto Metropolitan University. With over two decades of in
 dustry experience across North America\, she is recognized for her experti
 se in community-driven journalism\, news entrepreneurship and media innova
 tion. / anitali.me\n\nMatt Elliott has covered Toronto City Hall for more 
 than 15 years. Starting as a blogger\, he now contributes a column to the 
 Toronto Star and publishes City Hall Watcher\, an award-winning independen
 t newsletter providing in-depth news and analysis focused on the city’s 
 municipal government. / Bluesky\n\nLanrick Bennett Jr. is the Urbanist-in-
 Residence at the University of Toronto’s School of Cities and Toronto’
 s first Bicycle Mayor. Exploring the city with his kids has helped shape h
 is appreciation for the urban environment. His writing and research focus 
 on equitable mobility\, climate action\, inclusive city-building and munic
 ipal policy. / Bluesky\n\nA special agenda tonight:\n\n7:00-7:20 Welcome a
 nd Introductions\n\n7:20-8:30 Moderated discussion\n\n8:30-9:00 Mingling a
 nd informal breakouts\n\n‎\n\nCode of Conduct: https://civictech.ca/abou
 t-us\n\n‎\n\nCheck in with us on the Civic Tech Toronto Slack: https://l
 ink.civictech.ca/chat\n\n‎\n\nAbout Us:\n\nOur weekly civic meetups brin
 g together Torontonians (designers\, coders\, urban planners\, government 
 staff\, mappers\, policy-makers\, students\, communications strategists\, 
 community organizers\, and more) who share an interest in making Toronto m
 ore responsive\, prosperous\, sustainable\, and equitable through design\,
  tech\, and data.\n\nCome and be part of it!\n\nFor more info: https://civ
 ictech.ca\n\n\\--\n\nSuggest a Speaker:&#x20\;\n\nInterested in speaking a
 t a future event\, or know someone who'd be a great speaker? We'd love to 
 hear from you: https://link.civictech.ca/speaker-suggestions\n\nSuggest a 
 Venue:&#x20\;\n\nHave a space that could host up to 80 civic-minded folks 
 for an evening? Consider recommending your venue: https://link.civictech.c
 a/venue-suggestions\n
